Bug in my contract test: `guardIpcHandler` calls the handler with the raw payload then handler calls parse; calls.push happens before parse. So handler runs and rejects inside. The guard doesn't parse; the registry does. My test doesn't model the registry ordering (parse before handler). To assert "before the handler runs", use a function that parses first, like the registry:

```ts
const guarded = guardIpcHandler(entry.name, (e, value) => {
  const parsed = parseInvokePayload(key, value);
  calls.push(key);
  return parsed;
}, ...)
```
Then malformed throws in parse before calls.push. That models the registry. Fix.

Regex: `cp:validation` has only one segment. Use `/^cp:[a-z0-9]+(?::[a-z0-9]+)*$/`.

Fix test.

