App.tsx add handler + button. Add state? Simple synchronous note. Add function after onCancelReport:

```ts
async function onCopyDiagnostics(): Promise<void> {
  if (!bridge) {
    setNote('This page is open outside the ChessPulse window. Diagnostics are unavailable.');
    return;
  }
  try {
    await bridge.copyDiagnostics();
    setNote('Diagnostics copied. They contain no games, pulse samples, or keys.');
  } catch (caught: unknown) {
    setError(readIpcError(caught, 'internal'));
  }
}
```
Button at end of `.actions` div in main return:
```tsx
<button type="button" onClick={() => void onCopyDiagnostics()}>Copy diagnostics</button>
```
This appears in sensing too; fine.

Note: the note is status line; setting it after copy while sensing may be overwritten by `statusLine` (which ignores note during sensing unless no sdk error). Actually status = error ?? sdkError ?? statusLine(phase,...); statusLine ignores note for sensing. So confirmation won't show while sensing. Put the button only when phase !== 'sensing'? The diagnostics are most useful when something failed. But W4 will handle Help. For now, after copy set a dedicated state? Simpler: use `setNote` and it shows on idle/stopped; during sensing the status is sensing info. Could set a transient `copyNote` in the status priority? That touches BUG-11 territory (S46). Keep simple: button visible only when `phase !== 'sensing'` (idle/stopped). Hmm, a player may need diagnostics during a failure while sensing stopped—then stopped shows note. Fine.

Render button in actions when phase !== 'sensing'? There's already the Start button in the else branch. Add inside the `else` fragment? Current code:
```tsx
{phase === 'sensing' ? (...) : (
  <button Start .../>
)}
<button consent.../>
```
Add `<button ...>Copy diagnostics</button>` after consent so it's always available. Accept the note behavior. Or add `aria-live`? existing status.

I'll add always; if sensing, note won't display but error would. Could set error null on success? no.

Actually, to ensure feedback, introduce `const [copiedNote, setCopiedNote]`? Overkill. The plan's UI home is Help (S47). Fine.

Add handler and button.

