Node 20+ minimum; running Node 22. Use `MIN_NODE_MAJOR = 20`, pass if >= 20, fail otherwise.

Doctor checks details:

- node: label 'Node', status pass/fail, detail `v22.22.1 (needs 20 or newer)` or `v18.0.0 is older than 20`.
- env: `Title: '.env'`; if found: `Found; loaded N setting name(s): A, B` (names only). If not found: `Not found at <path>. Shell environment values are still used.` Status pass? If key missing, key check fails. Use `warn` when not found, because the file is optional if shell env set. Detail must include path? Path is local; okay but maybe no. Status warn.
  - loadedKeys is names only; max list maybe long. List sorted names.
- sensingKey: `SmartSpectra key`: present → pass `Present (value not shown).`; missing → fail `Missing. Set SMARTSPECTRA_API_KEY in .env or the environment.`
- camera: default skip `Camera enumeration runs inside the app window. The live result appears in Setup.`; in app S48 will inject. Wait — the plan says "camera enumerable where the platform allows". Maybe Electron main can use `systemPreferences.getMediaAccessStatus('camera')` on macOS/Windows. On Linux, Electron's `systemPreferences.getMediaAccessStatus` supports only macOS/Windows? Docs: 'camera' supported on macOS/Windows. We're on Linux. Skip. CLI skip. Fine.
- engine: probe; pass detail `Stockfish answered UCI and scored the start position.`; fail with reason.
- dataDir: writable → pass `Writable: <path>`? Avoid exposing home path? It's useful for support. Keep path. fail with error code (no secret).
- ai: `readAiConfig(env)`; configured → pass `Configured for openai with model X.`; disabled → warn `Off. <reason>` (reason may mention env var names, no values). AI is optional, so warn not fail.
- `ok` = no fail. Missing SmartSpectra key is fail (sensing requires it). Missing engine fail (report requires). Data dir fail. Node old fail.

`lines`: format `[status] Label: detail`? Diagnostics and CLI need readable. e.g.
```
PASS Node: v22.22.1 (needs 20 or newer)
PASS .env: found; loaded 2 names: CP_AI_KEY, SMARTSPECTRA_API_KEY
FAIL SmartSpectra key: missing...
SKIP Camera: ...
PASS Stockfish: ...
PASS Data directory: writable at ...
WARN AI reading: off — No AI key configured...
```
Use uppercase status. H-15 "never prints a secret" — the sensing key check never includes its value. The `.env` names include `SMARTSPECTRA_API_KEY`, which is a name not a value. Tests assert the secret value not in lines.

`runDoctor` implementation:
