```ts
it('allows a grounded measured heart-rate statement', () => {
  assert.equal(groundInsight({ bpm: 72 }, 'Your heart rate was 72.'), 'Your heart rate was 72.');
});
```
But the summary stats passed to the AI don't include a raw bpm? `computedSummary` includes baselineBpm, elevatedThresholdBpm, coverage etc. A model could say "your baseline heart rate was 70" — allowed if grounded. Fine.
- Add a test that "You have a heart condition" still blocked? `heart disease` catches "heart disease"; "condition" not. Not needed.

