const DEGREE = '(?:very |really |so |quite |extremely |incredibly |completely |totally |rather |pretty |somewhat |a bit |slightly |kind of |sort of |a little )?';
```
Regex with spaces. Build strings:
```ts
const STATE_MODIFIER = String.raw`(?:(?:very|really|so|quite|extremely|incredibly|completely|totally|rather|pretty|somewhat|a little|a bit|kind of|sort of|slightly)\s+)?`;
const STATE_ADJECTIVE = ...;
new RegExp(`\\byou(?:['’]re| are) ${STATE_MODIFIER}(?:anxious|...)\\b`, 'i')
```
Keep the array as RegExp literals? Easier to convert these three to `new RegExp` with constants. Ensure `noUnusedLocals` for constants used. Add a test in grounding.test.ts:
```ts
it('rejects a degree-modified direct state claim', () => {
  assert.throws(() => groundInsight({}, 'You were very stressed.'), /diagnostic or mental-state/);
});
it('still accepts pulse measurement', ...)
```
Maybe fixture-based is better but direct is fine. Also test "You seem really tired" etc.

